Both parts of the task are done and committed as 561025b5. The commit closes #1142 and #1138, citing yoagent 0.27.1. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings, the fmt check, neutered_guards and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

Step 4: I kept the TLS pre-flight. I switched it off temporarily, ran SSL_CERT_FILE=/dev/null yoyo -p hi, then switched it back on and confirmed main.rs was unchanged. With 0.27.1 there's no panic any more: yoyo exits 1 with yoagent's message, "cannot build the HTTP client (...). Usually the CA certificates: SSL_CERT_FILE / SSL_CERT_DIR, if set, must name PEM certificates…". That fixes the crash, but the pre-flight still does two things yoagent's message can't:
• Timing: yoagent builds its HTTP client fresh for each request (I read this in its source). So in the REPL its error only appears after the user has typed and sent a first turn. The pre-flight refuses at startup.
• Detail: yoagent can only name both variables as possibilities ("if set"). The pre-flight names the one actually set, its path and what's wrong, for example SSL_CERT_FILE is "/dev/null", which is empty.

The captured message and these reasons are now in tls_preflight.rs's module doc and in common-issues.md. A broken setup the pre-flight misses now gets yoagent's error, not a crash.

Step 5: a crashed agent is no longer reported as "reply cut off".
• What was wrong: when a turn's stream closed without its end event, yoyo always printed "reply cut off", including when the agent task had panicked.
• How it now tells them apart: main() installs a hook that counts panics and then hands off to the default hook, so panics still print exactly as before. It applies to every thread in the process but only counts. Each turn records the count when it starts, and a pure function, interrupt::classify_run_end, decides whether the turn finished, was cut short, or crashed.
• What the user sees: a crash now says "the agent crashed before finishing the turn: a panic, printed above … a bug in yoyo or yoagent, not a limit you hit; please report it". "Reply cut off" is only used when nothing panicked. Both still exit 1, and JSON output still reports is_error: true.
• Tests: a table drives classify_run_end directly (cut short, crashed, and finished even if something panicked). A second test spawns a real task that panics partway through a stream and checks the turn comes out as a crash. With the counter disabled that test failed by name (left: CutShort, right: Crashed); with it restored it passes.
• Docs: I updated the matching sentence in docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md, which described the old wording.

Issue references: the #1138 comments in main.rs, commands_git_review.rs and tls_preflight.rs now say it was fixed upstream in yoagent 0.27.1.

One limit: because the counter covers the whole process, a panic on an unrelated thread during a turn whose stream also dies would be reported as a crash. A panic really did happen in that case, so the message isn't false, but it may not be the agent's panic.
